{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2","id":783864,"title":"Table Size for NWod 2?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T19:37:46-08:00","id":783864,"title":"Table Size for NWod 2?","content":"Due to forces beyond my control I'm currently running with 6 players rather than my preferred 4. I'm thinking about running a WoD 2 game (Forsaken), but 6 seems like too many players, given that there is more RP and investigation in this kind of game than in a D&amp;D-type game (where you don't care if you have 9 people at the table since most of the time they're just stabbing stuff, not that there's anything wrong with that!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T02:41:53-08:00","id":784023,"title":"","content":"I ran with success a <b>Mage</b> chronicle of 6 player by the 2 years now. It is a bit &quot;crowdy&quot; but with individual Aspiration it is manageable. I have some advice for larger plays like those:<br /> <br /> 1. Make PCs center - the bigger &quot;main group&quot; focus, the better. I made 3 of 6 players &quot;chosen ones&quot; ( Hieromagus ) in game.<br /> 2. Use Aspirations - let players to choose one their own &quot;personal&quot;, one connected to chronicle storyline ( but still for the PC ), and one left free to declare in each game session. They will be pleased with this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Add Totem Aspiration to all, as it is<b> Forsaken</b> game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T03:29:18-08:00","id":784042,"title":"","content":"Clearly you're going to have to kick two people out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T03:50:40-08:00","id":784046,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is kinda built to work best with five players (Because auspices). Six probably wouldn't strain the system too much, but if you don't feel like you could juggle that many characters then don't push yourself. Stressed GMs are no fun for anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T04:31:41-08:00","id":784052,"title":"","content":"<b>Werewolf</b> is brutal game also - you must take in the account some characters can become really badly injured on the Hunt and be unable to participate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:40:30-08:00","id":784080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=784052#post784052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Werewolf</b> is brutal game also - you must take in the account some characters can become really badly injured on the Hunt and be unable to participate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't solve the problem of too many players... or at least it shouldn't. If a character is not able to participate for multiple sessions because of severe aggravated wounds, that isn't fun for the player. So I would try to give them an NPC to play so that they can still perform ingame interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2#post783864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to forces beyond my control I'm currently running with 6 players rather than my preferred 4. I'm thinking about running a WoD 2 game (Forsaken), but 6 seems like too many players, given that there is more RP and investigation in this kind of game than in a D&amp;D-type game (where you don't care if you have 9 people at the table since most of the time they're just stabbing stuff, not that there's anything wrong with that!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I'd recommend kicking at least one player out, but I understand that can be hard, especially when they are possibly your friends. In my experience, how many people one can handle also depends on how assertive the players play. If you have multiple quiet players who love to support the rest from the background and only intervene when it is their chance to shine, a larger group is possible.<br /> <br /> You could also discuss the problem with your players, and explain why you would prefer a smaller group. Maybe you and your groups can find ways to work around the problems without you having to stress out. For example, if your players accept that you will not be able to give them as much personal attention as you normally would, you won't have to be sorry when a player does not get the spotlight for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:51:10-08:00","id":784088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=784080#post784080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still doesn't solve the problem of too many players... or at least it shouldn't. If a character is not able to participate for multiple sessions because of severe aggravated wounds, that isn't fun for the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not say about couple sessions - rather one, two scenes. And <b>Werewolf</b> support NPC play by the Pack and Wolf-Blooded characters.<br /> <br /> Still, I also has lesser game problems as we often play in smaller group - <i>We made official schedule rule that we will play without one player</i>. Often it means that we play in 5 characters of out 6 PCs team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:54:45-08:00","id":784244,"title":"","content":"I think four really is the magic number with WoD. It's a reasonable group size to schedule, and when you split the characters up, it's easier not to have someone left alone (and bored). Also, someone told me once that the ideal rule of thumb for game length is an hour per player, plus one, though I've never quite been able to make that work.<br /> <br /> Five players is doable, but it stretches things.<br /> <br /> I ran a six player game a few years ago, and it was fun, but every session I felt like a player got left out. It was also very difficult to keep each character's backstory and plot line in mind. Basically, running a more focused, procedural type story (which is really WoD's bread and butter) became oppressively hard. Also, scheduling really was a nightmare.<br /> <br /> That's my experience, though, and it may say more about my organizational skills than anything...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T04:35:10-08:00","id":784652,"title":"","content":"From the newest <b>Chronicles of Darkness Corebook</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Individual gaming sessions, generally running two to four hours, are like weekly episodes. Secrets will be revealed, relationships will be tested, and blood will be spilled.Around two to five players take on one cast member each. You\u2019ll make decisions for your character. </div> </div> </div>I still much more like rule of the hand as &quot;one hour per player, plus one&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T01:45:18-08:00","id":785824,"title":"","content":"Currently I am running a 6 player Changeling game, and, while it is challenging, it works. First of all, I have made some of the individual aspirations part of the overall story, combining the backgrounds of several characters together. It means that I don't have to split time as much. Furthermore, I also discussed it with my players and they are well aware of the limitations and adapted their game play as well. They have a common goal, and they designed their characters as more willing to compromise if a choice has to be made between various plot lines. Of course, the presence of the Wyrd helps explaining some of the coincidences <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:31:08-08:00","id":785864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=784652#post784652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still much more like rule of the hand as &quot;one hour per player, plus one&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Are most peoples sessions actually that short?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:38:39-08:00","id":785870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=785864#post785864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Are most peoples sessions actually that short?</div> </div> </div> </div>New <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook have on start advice that game session is 2-4 hours, even if players are advised to be 2-5 group...<br /> <br /> Which I obviously disagree and pointed as possible bug in text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:43:31-08:00","id":785873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=785870#post785870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I obviously disagree and pointed as possible bug in text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know (though disagree that it's a bug, I think the dev's just disagree with you), I simply find that rule of hand of your's rather short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T03:46:39-08:00","id":785876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=785864#post785864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. Are most peoples sessions actually that short?</div> </div> </div> </div>As both a ST and a player, yeah. 4-5 hours was more than enough and we were all generally exhausted by the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:52:12-07:00","id":1077037,"title":"","content":"This is an old thread, But I want to bring it up again. I've been playing CoD with 5 for a while and I just got a 6th player. Any tips or the like? What are your guys table caps and experiences with large groups for CoD? How many players is CoD supposed to be played with ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:39:47-07:00","id":1077062,"title":"","content":"With any game system, 4 is my ideal number, 5 is fine, and 6 is the most I will run for. I've found with fewer players, you can afford to give each more individual attention and spotlight time without straining the others' attention spans. With six players, I try to focus on group activity as much as possible. Even if the group needs to split up for some reason, they should always be working at least in pairs so you're splitting spotlight time between three groups of two at the most, instead of six individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:27:38-07:00","id":1077128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=1077062#post1077062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With any game system, 4 is my ideal number, 5 is fine, and 6 is the most I will run for. I've found with fewer players, you can afford to give each more individual attention and spotlight time without straining the others' attention spans. With six players, I try to focus on group activity as much as possible. Even if the group needs to split up for some reason, they should always be working at least in pairs so you're splitting spotlight time between three groups of two at the most, instead of six individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean we are playing an online game, and I do worry about causing the spotlight to be split so many ways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. But at the sametime, It's a very unusual crossover game - Currently the party consist of 2 Kindred, an Unchained, a Mage, a Mummy, and an Inferno 1E (2e homebrewed) Les Miserables, so it's been a very interesting game so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. My worry is just being able to get better as a storyteller and streamline things better along with get the group to unite more often since people often go on their own paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:25:48-07:00","id":1078394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783864-table-size-for-nwod-2?p=785864#post785864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. Are most peoples sessions actually that short?</div> </div> </div> </div>Our games ran more to 10-11 hours per session as our norm. Saturdays From 1300 to 2300 or so... generally 4-5 players, though we did swell to 7 at one point over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:00: